1013
01:06:29,140 --> 01:06:31,140
There's no way. “Husband”?

1014
01:06:31,140 --> 01:06:33,840
“Husband.” Nobody would let that slip.

1015
01:06:33,840 --> 01:06:34,320
No one.

1016
01:06:34,320 --> 01:06:36,320
Who would say that?

1017
01:06:36,320 --> 01:06:38,320
[Laughter]

1018
01:06:38,320 --> 01:06:40,320
Surely it didn't happen.

1019
01:06:40,320 --> 01:06:42,320
Nobody would say something like that.

1020
01:06:42,320 --> 01:06:44,320
[Laughter]

1021
01:06:44,320 --> 01:06:46,320
And yet someone did.

1022
01:06:46,320 --> 01:06:48,320
Seriously.

1023
01:06:48,320 --> 01:06:49,320
Now then.

1024
01:06:49,320 --> 01:06:50,320
There's simply no way.

1025
01:06:50,320 --> 01:06:54,320
Lulu-chan, do you think this is true or false?

1026
01:06:54,320 --> 01:06:58,320
I think it is... true.

1027
01:06:58,320 --> 01:07:00,320
Surely...

1028
01:07:00,320 --> 01:07:01,320
I know this one.

1029
01:07:01,320 --> 01:07:02,320
Of course you knew.

1030
01:07:02,320 --> 01:07:03,320
I did.

1031
01:07:03,320 --> 01:07:05,320
Of course I knew this one.

1032
01:07:05,320 --> 01:07:09,320
Here is the correct answer.

1033
01:07:09,320 --> 01:07:13,320
It is true! Thank you.

1034
01:07:13,320 --> 01:07:15,320
What a story.

1035
01:07:15,320 --> 01:07:29,320
A Nijisanji Liver named Hayase Sou casually let “my husband” slip, and didn't even notice during the stream.

1036
01:07:29,320 --> 01:07:31,320
That's wild—“husband.”

1037
01:07:31,320 --> 01:07:38,320
In her next stream, she confessed that she actually had a boyfriend.

1038
01:07:38,320 --> 01:07:41,320
The amazing part is that he wasn't actually her husband, but her boyfriend.

1039
01:07:41,320 --> 01:07:43,320
She called her boyfriend “husband.”

1040
01:07:43,320 --> 01:07:46,320
That was revealed too.

1041
01:07:46,320 --> 01:07:51,320
So many things were revealed at once.

1042
01:07:51,320 --> 01:07:52,320
Still, it was peaceful.

1043
01:07:52,320 --> 01:07:58,320
People made a fairly good-natured fuss, which made it amusing.

1044
01:07:58,320 --> 01:08:00,320
It really was remarkable.

1045
01:08:00,320 --> 01:08:01,320
[Laughter]

1046
01:08:01,320 --> 01:08:03,320
Naturally, you knew that one.

1047
01:08:03,320 --> 01:08:05,320
Yes, of course.

1048
01:08:05,320 --> 01:08:10,320
Then perhaps the next one can fool you.

1049
01:08:10,320 --> 01:08:14,320
Here is the next story.

1050
01:08:14,320 --> 01:08:15,320
Ta-da!

1051
01:08:15,320 --> 01:08:17,320
Here we go.

1052
01:08:17,320 --> 01:08:27,320
“Yaguruma Rine was exposed as living in Australia by a speed-test screen during a game stream and a new feature in X.”

1053
01:08:27,320 --> 01:08:29,320
